      "beat_id": "B03",
      "act": "WORKED_EXAMPLE",
      "narration_text": "I ran it. At temperature point five, dividing makes the gaps between scores bigger. Mat jumps to eighty-six percent. Sofa twelve. Roof two. Moon rounds to zero. The model will say mat almost every time. That's what you want for facts, code, or anything that should come out the same twice.",
