    {
      "beat_id": "B05",
      "act": "FALSIFIABILITY",
      "narration_text": "So the practical rule. Low temperature for facts, code, and extraction, where you want the same reliable answer. Higher temperature for brainstorming and stories, where variety is the point. But remember the moon. Turning temperature up never adds knowledge. It just gives unlikely words more chances, and some of those are wrong.",
